  "name": "Fantasy Keep",
  "category": "Fantasy",
  "blurb": "A battered stone keep with arrow slits, twisted out of true.",
  "teach": "Defensive architecture and fantasy architecture want the same two things: mass at the bottom and almost no openings. The batter gives the thickened base, the arrow slits are an ordinary Facade with the window width dropped to half a metre and the pier widened past it, and a Twist deform rotates each storey a little against the one below so the keep looks hand-piled rather than extruded. The twist is seeded from the document, so it is the same crooked tower every time.",
